        "content": "<p>netliomax25-code opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15196\">PR #15196</a> from <code>netliomax25-code:wasi-tls-p3-flush-after-write</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>AsyncWriteConsumer</code> in the p3 wasi-tls host never flushed the <code>AsyncWrite</code> it writes to. <code>connector.send</code> uses it to write the guest's cleartext into the TLS stream, and tokio-rustls's <code>poll_write</code> hands the plaintext to rustls, writes TLS records to the transport until it would block, then returns <code>Ok(n)</code> with the rest still queued in rustls. Those records only go out on a later write, flush or shutdown. The transport is the 16 KiB ciphertext pipe, so when a guest makes one write of more than about 16 KiB (say an HTTP request with a 17 KB body) and then waits for the response, the peer never gets a complete record and both sides wait.</p>\n<p>The consumer now flushes after each write and keeps the write pending until the flush finishes, the same way <code>OutputStreamConsumer</code> in wasmtime-wasi's p3 CLI host does. On the receive side the consumer writes into the in-memory pipe, where flushing is a no-op.</p>\n<p>To reproduce I drove the real <code>send</code>/<code>receive</code>/<code>connect</code> host functions against an in-process rustls server, with one cleartext write and the stream left open afterward. 1000 and 16000 bytes arrived; 17000 and 40960 bytes arrived as 0. With this change all four arrive in full. The unit test added here uses an <code>AsyncWrite</code> that only passes data on when flushed, and it fails without the change. <code>cargo test -p wasmtime-wasi-tls --features nativetls</code>, clippy and the per-feature checks pass locally. I couldn't build the <code>openssl</code> provider here, but the change doesn't touch the providers.</p>\n<p>wasi-tls is tier 3, so I don't think this falls under the security policy. I didn't find an existing issue for it.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 638402070,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794076557
    },
